q(STATE,"2.2.2","NMLS registry","easy","recall","The NMLS serves as:",["A lender that funds loans","The system of record for licensing and registration of MLOs across states","A credit bureau","An appraisal firm"],1,"The Nationwide Multistate Licensing System is the system of record through which MLOs are licensed/registered and through which states coordinate supervision. Consumer Access lets the public verify originators.","12 U.S.C. \u00a75101 et seq.")
q(STATE,"2.2.5","Dual compensation","hard","application-scenario","Under the LO compensation rule, an originator generally may not:",["Be paid a salary","Receive compensation from both the consumer and another person on the same transaction","Be paid per loan","Earn a commission"],1,"The rule prohibits dual compensation, an originator receiving pay from both the consumer and another party (like the creditor) on the same transaction. Salary, per-loan, and permissible commissions are allowed.","Regulation Z, 12 CFR \u00a71026.36(d)(2)")
q(STATE,"2.3.2","Licensed services","medium","recall","A licensed MLO is authorized to:",["Perform appraisals","Take applications and offer or negotiate residential mortgage loan terms","Issue title insurance","Practice law"],1,"An MLO license authorizes taking applications and offering/negotiating residential mortgage terms. Appraising, title insurance, and legal practice require separate credentials.","12 U.S.C. \u00a75102(4)")
q(STATE,"2.3.4","Entities needing MLO","medium","application-scenario","A nondepository mortgage company that originates residential loans must:",["Employ or contract licensed MLOs and hold the required company license","Operate without any license","Use only registered (depository) MLOs","Hold only a real estate license"],0,"Nondepository lenders and brokers must hold the required state company license and ensure their originators are licensed MLOs under Regulation H. Depository registration (Reg G) is a separate regime.","12 CFR Part 1008 (Reg H)")
q(STATE,"2.3.7","Retake waiting period","medium","recall","After failing the SAFE MLO test, a candidate must wait how long before the next attempt (first through third fails)?",["24 hours","30 days","6 months","1 year"],1,"After each of the first three failures, a candidate must wait 30 days before retaking. After three consecutive failures, the wait is 180 days.","NMLS Testing Handbook, test retake policy")
q(STATE,"2.3.8","Sponsorship","medium","application-scenario","An MLO's license is generally not active to originate until:",["They pass the test","They are sponsored by a licensed employer in NMLS","They complete CE","They post a bond"],1,"Even with an approved license, an MLO typically cannot originate until an employer sponsors them through NMLS, linking the individual license to the licensed company.","NMLS sponsorship requirement; state law")
q(STATE,"2.3.9","MLO definition","easy","recall","Under the SAFE Act, a mortgage loan originator is someone who, for compensation:",["Only processes paperwork","Takes a residential mortgage application AND offers or negotiates terms","Appraises property","Records deeds"],1,"An MLO both takes a residential mortgage loan application and offers or negotiates terms of a residential mortgage loan for compensation or gain. Doing only one, or purely clerical work, generally does not meet the definition.","12 U.S.C. \u00a75102(4)")
q(STATE,"2.3.10","License denial grounds","medium","recall","A state may deny an MLO license for:",["Having any debt","A disqualifying criminal history or failure to demonstrate financial responsibility/character","Being a first-time applicant","Working part-time"],1,"Grounds for denial include disqualifying criminal history, failure to meet financial-responsibility or character-and-fitness standards, or providing false information, not simply having debt or being new.","12 U.S.C. \u00a75104")
q(STATE,"2.3.12","Change of employment","medium","application-scenario","When a licensed MLO changes employers, they must:",["Retake the SAFE test","Update their NMLS record and obtain new sponsorship","Get a new SSN","Redo pre-licensing education"],1,"A change of employer requires updating the NMLS record and obtaining sponsorship by the new employer; the license and test do not need to be redone for the move.","NMLS transition requirements")
q(STATE,"2.4.5","Permissible act","medium","application-scenario","Which is a permissible act for a licensed MLO?",["Using a borrower's info without authorization","Disclosing their NMLS ID and providing accurate disclosures","Steering for higher pay","Splitting unearned fees"],1,"Providing the NMLS identifier and accurate, required disclosures is permissible and expected. Unauthorized use of borrower information, steering, and unearned-fee splitting are prohibited.","12 CFR \u00a71008.107; RESPA/Reg Z")
q(STATE,"2.4.6","Penalties","medium","recall","Failure to comply with state mortgage law may result in:",["A thank-you letter","Fines, license suspension or revocation, and other enforcement action","Automatic license renewal","A higher commission"],1,"Noncompliance can lead to civil penalties, license suspension or revocation, cease-and-desist orders, and restitution, depending on the violation and state law.","State Model Law enforcement provisions")

# calc top-up (monthly payment via factor, plus a few more)
def money(n): return "${:,.0f}".format(n)
def money2(n): return "${:,.2f}".format(n)
def mc(correct, distractors, fmt):
    import random as _r
    opts=[correct]+distractors; _r.shuffle(opts); return [fmt(o) for o in opts], opts.index(correct)
# simple down-payment-percent-from-dollars
for _ in range(5):
    price=random.choice([250000,300000,320000,360000,400000]); dpd=random.choice([25000,30000,40000,50000,60000])
    correct=round(dpd/price*100,1)
    opts,ci=mc(correct,[round(correct*1.2,1),round(correct*0.8,1),round(100-correct,1)],lambda o:f"{o}%")
    B.append({"content_area":ORIG,"outline_ref":"4.4.3","subtopic":"Calculations - down payment %","difficulty":"easy","type":"calculation",
      "stem":f"A buyer pays {money(dpd)} down on a {money(price)} home. What down-payment percentage is that?","options":opts,"correct_index":ci,
      "explanation":f"Down payment % = down / price = {money(dpd)} / {money(price)} = {correct}%.","primary_source_citation":"Standard purchase calculation","last_reviewed_date":TODAY})
# monthly interest portion (first month)
for _ in range(5):
    loan=random.choice([200000,250000,300000,325000,360000]); rate=random.choice([0.05,0.055,0.06,0.065,0.07])
    correct=round(loan*rate/12,2)
    opts,ci=mc(correct,[round(correct*1.1,2),round(correct*0.9,2),round(loan*rate/360,2)],money2)
    B.append({"content_area":ORIG,"outline_ref":"4.4.1","subtopic":"Calculations - monthly interest","difficulty":"medium","type":"calculation",
      "stem":f"On a {money(loan)} loan at {rate*100:.2f}%, how much of the first monthly payment is interest?","options":opts,"correct_index":ci,
      "explanation":f"First-month interest = balance x rate / 12 = {money(loan)} x {rate:.4f} / 12 = {money2(correct)}.","primary_source_citation":"Standard amortization","last_reviewed_date":TODAY})

# ---- merge + re-id ----
data=json.load(open(os.path.join(HERE,"questions.json")))
allq=data["questions"]+B
order={FED:1,STATE:2,GEN:3,ORIG:4,ETH:5}
allq.sort(key=lambda x:(order[x["content_area"]],x["outline_ref"]))
for i,q_ in enumerate(allq,1): q_["id"]=f"Q{i:04d}"
data["questions"]=allq; data["meta"]["total"]=len(allq); data["meta"]["version"]="0.4"
json.dump(data,open(os.path.join(HERE,"questions.json"),"w"),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)
print(f"Batch 2 added {len(B)} questions. New total: {len(allq)}")
